    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:c3205ac1e20a266d",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "10ea7ddce592ee70a7468d50b69f1b1d55f0fd08341650583de8be7d0181b59c",
      "text": "Day 9 · Morning departure from Salta for Purmamarca (approx. 4 hours) and excursion through the Quebrada de Humahuaca, a UNESCO World Heritage Site for its marvellous landscapes and more than 10,000 years of history, with indigenous fortresses, prehistoric caves, hamlets and pre-Columbian and colonial settlements.\n\nIn Purmamarca, admire the Hill of Seven Colours and the old Church of Santa Rosa de Lima. Continue to Tilcara and its ancient indigenous fortress, then to Uquía, whose church holds one of the most important collections of the famous arquebusier angels. The visit ends in Humahuaca, on the banks of the Río Grande, with its narrow cobbled streets and colonial monuments.",
      "provenance": {
